        "invention-title": {
         "$": "BED SYSTEM HAVING FEATURES FOR DETERMINING PPG, SPO2, AND/OR HYPOXIA BURDEN FROM A BCG SIGNAL",
         "@lang": "en"
        }
       },
       "abstract": {
        "@lang": "en",
        "p": {
         "$": "A bed has a mattress. A user sensor is configured to: sense a user on the bed; and transmit, to a computing system, a user stream from the sensing of the user on the bed. The computing system including at least one processor and memory, the computing system configured to: receive the user stream; generate, from the user stream, a plurality of time-shifted balistocardiography (BCG) data steams; for a first time window: submit the plurality of time-shifted BCG data streams to a photoplethysmography (PPG) synthesizer; and receive, from the PPG synthesizer, a PPG value for the user for the first time window."
        }
       }
      }
