        },
        "invention-title": {
         "$": "METHOD FOR MONITORING BLOOD PRESSURE",
         "@lang": "en"
        }
       },
       "abstract": {
        "@lang": "en",
        "p": {
         "$": "[0000]    Methods and systems are provided herein for measuring a blood pressure (BP) of a subject when continuous monitoring is desired, and a traditional cuff-based blood pressure measurement system may be restrictive. The proposed systems and methods measure the BP using dual photoplethysmography (PPG) sensors integrated into the cuff, which can dramatically reduce the frequency of cuff inflation while providing continuous BP monitoring. The dual PPG sensors monitor a BP of a patient by calculating a Pulse Wave Velocity (PWV) of blood in a blood vessel of the patient based on a Pulse Transit Time (PTT), and an PPG Intensity Ratio (PIR). The patient's BP may be measured continuously based on these physiological parameters, with the cuff serving as a reference to periodically recalibrate the system automatically, thereby enhancing accuracy and reducing a demand for frequent cuff inflation."
        }
       }
      }
     }
    ]
   }
